WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:01.450
- Welcome back, everyone,

00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:03.550
to my channel here on Firm Learning.

00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:06.670
This is the Christmas
edition of Firm Learning.

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:09.000
So welcome to another coffee break indeed,

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.180
and Merry Christmas to all of you.

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:15.940
I feel honored that today I
have my sister with me here.

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:17.380
- Yes, hi. I'm Carolina.

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:18.590
I'm Heinrich's sister,

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:20.970
and I'm joining him for this new video.

00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:21.803
I'm excited.

00:00:21.803 --> 00:00:23.320
- The first time on the channel,

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:24.440
So it's a pleasure, Carolina.

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:26.320
Please be nice to her in the comments,

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:28.190
because what we have
planned here for today

00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:30.330
is a little Christmas edition,

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:32.010
a person in edition.

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:34.720
I hope that this would help
you better get to know me,

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:35.800
and also the other way around

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:38.300
if we have some conversations
about this in the comments.

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:40.830
Because what I asked you
to do on the Instagram

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:43.810
is to ask me a couple
of personal questions,

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:47.510
personal things that you would
like to know about myself.

00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:49.370
and I screenshotted all the answers

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:51.000
and sent them to Carolina,

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.140
so she has them all on her phone now.

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:56.830
And so I trust she will now
pick a couple of the questions

00:00:56.830 --> 00:00:58.290
that you sent me,

00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:00.823
and let's see what I will answer to that.

00:01:00.823 --> 00:01:03.860
And Carolina, you agree that
you didn't tell him in advance

00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:05.240
what questions these will be, right?

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:06.250
- No, I didn't tell him in advance,

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:09.560
so it's gonna be a
little surprise for him.

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:10.393
- Surprise, surprise.

00:01:10.393 --> 00:01:11.829
So let's go.
- So let's start.

00:01:11.829 --> 00:01:12.910
- Indeed.

00:01:12.910 --> 00:01:14.287
- First question,

00:01:14.287 --> 00:01:17.517
"Who inspires you for your
success and creativity?"

00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:20.700
- Oh, that's a good one.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:21.870
And here, frankly,

00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:23.910
I think there many
people who do inspire me,

00:01:23.910 --> 00:01:26.890
probably both on the personal
and on the professional side.

00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:29.420
So I had the pleasure to work

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:32.860
with some extremely
inspirational, motivational people

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:35.060
over the course of my
career over the last years.

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:37.160
And I don't wanna say any specific names,

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:39.950
but there were several past colleagues

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:42.230
or some project leads of
mine, partners of mine,

00:01:42.230 --> 00:01:43.460
that I worked with,

00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:46.450
and that I really enjoyed
working with a lot.

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:49.210
Some other friends of mine
who I meet at university

00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:50.330
who I regularly see,

00:01:50.330 --> 00:01:52.520
founded some startups, other careers,

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:54.650
are some very inspirational people.

00:01:54.650 --> 00:01:56.250
And for sure, lots of things

00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:59.200
that have come from these
gentlemen and ladies in the past.

00:02:00.690 --> 00:02:02.703
- How did your first marathon go?

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:06.680
- My first marathon was, I believe,

00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:10.450
2017 or 2018 or so in Paris.

00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:13.620
So I ran the marathon in Paris there.

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:17.210
I wasn't much of a runner before.

00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:20.480
The furthest thing that I could
do were maybe 10 kilometers

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:22.100
or something like that.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:23.730
But that was quite a stretch for me.

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:26.550
And then it was actually
my wife who motivated me

00:02:26.550 --> 00:02:28.270
to do a half marathon.

00:02:28.270 --> 00:02:31.420
She was always much more of
a runner than I always was.

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:32.530
And so then I remember

00:02:32.530 --> 00:02:34.520
that about a year before this marathon,

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:37.410
we signed up for a half
marathon in Munich,

00:02:37.410 --> 00:02:40.200
and I managed to do that then as well.

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:41.870
And then I got some confidence

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:43.980
that probably if I could
do the half marathon,

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:46.480
I would also be able to
then run the extra marathon.

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:47.840
And so over the course of a year,

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:50.470
I did some training, practiced.

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:52.540
And in the end, yes, I made it in Paris.

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:55.740
And then one year later I
ran the marathon in Munich.

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:58.230
And then I wanted to
then also the year after

00:02:58.230 --> 00:02:59.200
do another marathon.

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:02.090
So my idea was to run
my one marathon a year,

00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:05.000
but then the whole health
situation prevented that.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:06.930
And then the marathon got canceled.

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:08.780
Now, frankly, I'm a
little bit out of shape.

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:11.640
So probably for the New Year
resolutions for next year,

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:13.920
this is one of the
things I need to tackle.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:17.300
- So how many marathons
did you do in total now?

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:18.133
- Two.

00:03:18.133 --> 00:03:19.066
- Two, okay.

00:03:19.066 --> 00:03:19.899
- But Carolina, I know

00:03:19.899 --> 00:03:21.883
that you are also currently
running a lot yourself,

00:03:22.730 --> 00:03:25.450
so probably some things that
I should learn from you again,

00:03:25.450 --> 00:03:26.500
inspired from you.

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:29.158
- But pretty far away
from a marathon, I think.

00:03:29.158 --> 00:03:30.130
- Baby steps.

00:03:30.130 --> 00:03:30.963
- Yes.

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:34.359
So you spoke about your wife already.

00:03:34.359 --> 00:03:35.192
So now the question

00:03:35.192 --> 00:03:37.190
I think everyone was kind
of asking themselves,

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:39.610
how did you find your wife?

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:42.220
- Yeah, so I'm together with my now wife

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:43.700
already for many, many years.

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:47.050
I met her in the beginning of university,

00:03:47.050 --> 00:03:50.440
and it was actually on Odeonsplatz,

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:52.280
which was quite a big place.

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:53.480
Everybody from Munich would know it.

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:56.100
And I met her actually after Oktoberfest.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:57.330
So I was on Oktoberfest,

00:03:57.330 --> 00:03:59.080
you know how this goes.

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:01.900
Like leather trousers,
some beer and so on.

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:03.730
And then after, once we left,

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:04.990
and then we were on on Odeonsplatz

00:04:04.990 --> 00:04:09.630
and then I saw a random group
of ladies standing there.

00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:12.020
I was with some friends myself as well.

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:13.540
And then we approached them,

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:16.940
and this is how I got to know my now wife.

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:18.592
- So you just talked to her.

00:04:18.592 --> 00:04:21.020
- I just talked to her with
a little bit of confidence

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:24.820
from drinking the one or
other Mass at Oktoberfest.

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:28.130
The locals know what I'm talking about.

00:04:28.130 --> 00:04:29.590
That gave me then the confidence

00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:31.520
to approach them and talk to her.

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:34.190
And yes, many, many years ago.

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:37.940
And then two or three years
ago now, we got married.

00:04:37.940 --> 00:04:39.620
- So how many years ago was that?

00:04:39.620 --> 00:04:40.453
- In 2019.

00:04:40.453 --> 00:04:42.173
- 2019. Nice.

00:04:44.020 --> 00:04:45.010
It's a German question.

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:50.010
So "Which topic are you
educating yourself on currently?"

00:04:51.890 --> 00:04:54.097
- So that's a good question.

00:04:54.097 --> 00:04:57.480
And I mean, during my current
role at Building Radar

00:04:57.480 --> 00:05:00.170
where I currently work as
a chief revenue officer,

00:05:00.170 --> 00:05:03.230
one of the topics that now
I'm focusing more about,

00:05:03.230 --> 00:05:04.830
which of course also heavily relates

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:07.520
to what I do at Firm
Learning, is online marketing.

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:10.620
So I'm currently learning a
lot about online marketing,

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:15.600
copywriting, creating sales
funnels, sales structures.

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:17.530
This of course is a big,
important topic also

00:05:17.530 --> 00:05:18.940
for Building Radar and what we do here

00:05:18.940 --> 00:05:20.170
at Firm Learning as well.

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:22.130
So yeah, currently lots of books

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:25.720
under my bed about these topics.

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:27.900
- And you like to listen to them, right?

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:30.540
- Some are also on Audible.

00:05:30.540 --> 00:05:32.860
This is a service that
I use to listen to them,

00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:36.390
but some also in the
written, printed book format.

00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:37.223
- Nice.

00:05:38.057 --> 00:05:40.407
"What brings you joy in life?"

00:05:41.410 --> 00:05:42.550
- Oh, wow.

00:05:42.550 --> 00:05:44.890
That's a philosophical question.

00:05:44.890 --> 00:05:49.870
And even though I did study
philosophy many, many years ago

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:51.070
and I have a Bachelor of Philosophy,

00:05:51.070 --> 00:05:52.210
I think this is a question

00:05:52.210 --> 00:05:53.810
that's often very difficult to answer.

00:05:53.810 --> 00:05:56.520
But in my specific situation,

00:05:56.520 --> 00:05:59.750
given that this year
our baby girl was born,

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:02.270
the answer is of course quite easy.

00:06:02.270 --> 00:06:03.700
So we feel so blessed

00:06:03.700 --> 00:06:06.450
that since April actually of this year,

00:06:06.450 --> 00:06:09.380
we have a baby girl that's
part of our young family.

00:06:09.380 --> 00:06:12.160
And of course, she brings
us joy every single day,

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:13.840
even though it's of
course not always easy.

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:16.640
It's sometimes also quite tiring.

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:19.067
She's more than making up for that.

00:06:19.067 --> 00:06:21.020
- "What have you learned about yourself

00:06:21.950 --> 00:06:23.847
since having your daughter?"

00:06:25.640 --> 00:06:26.473
- What do you think about that?

00:06:26.473 --> 00:06:29.103
Did they change in any way
since I have a daughter?

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:31.133
- Not really, I think.

00:06:31.133 --> 00:06:33.357
I think you're still the same.

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:38.120
Not much, actually. No.

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:40.380
- Yeah, I mean, it's an
interesting question.

00:06:40.380 --> 00:06:44.790
So do we change because
we become children?

00:06:44.790 --> 00:06:47.420
I mean, surely your priorities shift,

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:50.490
and surely this is a new,
big responsibility of course

00:06:50.490 --> 00:06:52.210
that you have in your life.

00:06:52.210 --> 00:06:54.993
And surely now, you have
to think about new things

00:06:54.993 --> 00:06:57.650
that you didn't need to
think about in the past.

00:06:57.650 --> 00:06:59.020
So a couple of days before,

00:06:59.020 --> 00:07:01.050
we decided to actually take the train here

00:07:01.050 --> 00:07:02.080
to the west of Germany.

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:04.020
Our girl was sick, so we wondered,

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:05.740
can we now do the train ride

00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:06.940
because she wasn't feeling well.

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:09.110
And thankfully she recovered in time.

00:07:09.110 --> 00:07:11.900
Of course, this is a
new layer of complexity

00:07:11.900 --> 00:07:13.610
that we didn't have before.

00:07:13.610 --> 00:07:17.580
But I must say, beyond these
smallest, obvious things,

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:20.350
I don't feel like life
completely changed for me

00:07:20.350 --> 00:07:22.057
to be honest now.

00:07:22.057 --> 00:07:25.020
- "What's your advice on work-life balance

00:07:25.020 --> 00:07:28.967
and balancing career
aspirations with family needs?"

00:07:30.230 --> 00:07:31.063
- I mean, here for sure,

00:07:31.063 --> 00:07:31.940
this is one of the things

00:07:31.940 --> 00:07:33.817
where your perspective does change also

00:07:33.817 --> 00:07:35.310
after you become children.

00:07:35.310 --> 00:07:38.187
So I remember when I was
working in consulting,

00:07:38.187 --> 00:07:40.840
it was very common for
me, no problem at all,

00:07:40.840 --> 00:07:44.390
to obviously work late in the evenings.

00:07:44.390 --> 00:07:47.960
I remember my first internship
that I did in consulting,

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:49.510
I spend with the team in the office.

00:07:49.510 --> 00:07:51.220
That was like the first or second day.

00:07:51.220 --> 00:07:53.180
And then around 7:00 or 8:00 PM,

00:07:53.180 --> 00:07:55.272
we decided to go for some dinner.

00:07:55.272 --> 00:07:56.530
I thought, yeah, sure, why not?

00:07:56.530 --> 00:07:58.770
Let's have some dinner with the team.

00:07:58.770 --> 00:08:01.630
And then I was eating something.

00:08:01.630 --> 00:08:03.630
And then I must say I was
a little bit surprised

00:08:03.630 --> 00:08:04.710
that then after dinner,

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:06.720
everyone was going back to the team room.

00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:08.550
So we were going back to the team room.

00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:10.090
We continuing to work there.

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:11.890
Probably this was just
a sign of my ignorance,

00:08:11.890 --> 00:08:13.210
that I didn't inform myself enough

00:08:13.210 --> 00:08:15.720
before I applied for this
consulting internship.

00:08:16.700 --> 00:08:18.340
But at that time, that was normal.

00:08:18.340 --> 00:08:19.990
It wasn't a problem at all for me.

00:08:19.990 --> 00:08:22.110
And frankly, I know many
people also with family

00:08:22.110 --> 00:08:24.450
than decide to continue this career path.

00:08:24.450 --> 00:08:27.750
but the truth is of course
that many people also,

00:08:27.750 --> 00:08:28.820
once they get children,

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:32.080
then at some point decide
that maybe this is the time

00:08:32.080 --> 00:08:34.610
to spend a little bit more
time at home with your family,

00:08:34.610 --> 00:08:35.443
with their children.

00:08:35.443 --> 00:08:39.270
Because of course it's great
to see them during the week,

00:08:39.270 --> 00:08:40.880
see them in the evenings.

00:08:40.880 --> 00:08:44.520
And this was not the main
reason why I left the firm,

00:08:44.520 --> 00:08:45.850
the consulting firm,

00:08:45.850 --> 00:08:48.240
because that was already
when I didn't have a child.

00:08:48.240 --> 00:08:50.330
But surely now, thinking back

00:08:50.330 --> 00:08:51.970
at when I was still working in consulting

00:08:51.970 --> 00:08:53.620
or having a child at the same time,

00:08:53.620 --> 00:08:56.307
that that would have been quite difficult.

00:08:58.972 --> 00:09:02.690
- So then this is like
three questions in one.

00:09:02.690 --> 00:09:04.190
First, "What drives you?"

00:09:04.190 --> 00:09:06.730
Second, "What are your pillars?"

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:09.070
And three, "How do these pillars

00:09:09.070 --> 00:09:11.227
impact you and your decisions?"

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:15.027
- Here probably also the truth

00:09:15.027 --> 00:09:19.880
is it's not that I have these
big drivers where I could say,

00:09:19.880 --> 00:09:22.300
this is why I do the things that I do.

00:09:22.300 --> 00:09:24.370
The pillars, if you mean this,

00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:27.450
like the virtues, the
values that drive you,

00:09:27.450 --> 00:09:28.830
so here I think I would struggle.

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:31.050
But one thing that I really liked,

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:32.300
it's part of an organization

00:09:32.300 --> 00:09:34.030
I was part of as a student.

00:09:34.030 --> 00:09:36.110
In German, you say, (in foreign language).

00:09:40.475 --> 00:09:43.100
I feel like this is quite
a strong group of words.

00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:45.950
So (in foreign language) means probably-

00:09:45.950 --> 00:09:47.828
- Performance.
- Performance.

00:09:47.828 --> 00:09:50.340
(in foreign language)
means drive, initiative.

00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:52.890
And (in foreign language)
means responsibility.

00:09:52.890 --> 00:09:56.250
I find these three pretty
good and sound principles

00:09:56.250 --> 00:09:57.230
that you wanna follow.

00:09:57.230 --> 00:09:58.990
So of course the things that you do

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:01.600
you wanna do well, performance.

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:02.830
you don't just wanna do the things

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:03.680
that you are asked to do,

00:10:03.680 --> 00:10:06.390
but also have some
initiative, be proactive.

00:10:06.390 --> 00:10:07.780
Think about, try to be yourself.

00:10:07.780 --> 00:10:10.290
What are the things that
you wanna shape and build

00:10:10.290 --> 00:10:11.450
and create in your life?

00:10:11.450 --> 00:10:13.420
And then third, of course, responsibility.

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:15.660
At some point, that's the question.

00:10:15.660 --> 00:10:19.420
I are responsible of course
for your family, for society.

00:10:19.420 --> 00:10:21.350
Can you transform the things that you do

00:10:21.350 --> 00:10:24.560
to become the force
for good, in any sense?

00:10:24.560 --> 00:10:28.333
I think these are questions
very well worth to be inquired.

00:10:29.340 --> 00:10:32.396
- Nice. Something I
can learn here as well.

00:10:32.396 --> 00:10:34.917
- (faintly speaking) that you can.

00:10:34.917 --> 00:10:39.050
- "Your Patagonia vest,
which one do you recommend?"

00:10:39.050 --> 00:10:41.740
- So I think yesterday I
posted an Instagram Story,

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:43.810
and then I got some questions
on this new Patagonia vest.

00:10:43.810 --> 00:10:47.500
Indeed, my wife gave this to
me as a Christmas present.

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:49.600
So see here, I'm not
sure if you can see it,

00:10:49.600 --> 00:10:52.753
the sort of Firm Learning embroidery here.

00:10:54.080 --> 00:10:57.360
So I like Patagonia vests quite a lot,

00:10:57.360 --> 00:10:58.540
but I feel like at some point,

00:10:58.540 --> 00:11:00.190
especially over the last one or two years,

00:11:00.190 --> 00:11:03.860
I'm a bit afraid they
became even more of a cliche

00:11:03.860 --> 00:11:06.460
than they already were a cliche.

00:11:06.460 --> 00:11:08.450
So I'm not sure if I can really continue.

00:11:08.450 --> 00:11:09.549
- Maybe you shake the cliche.

00:11:09.549 --> 00:11:10.520
I'm not trying.

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:13.430
- I don't know, but I
think they look cool.

00:11:13.430 --> 00:11:16.650
It's also really nice under a suit, maybe.

00:11:16.650 --> 00:11:19.720
Also in the team room in
consulting, just to stay warm.

00:11:19.720 --> 00:11:22.190
Then at some point you can take away

00:11:22.190 --> 00:11:24.960
like the upper part of your suit,

00:11:24.960 --> 00:11:27.660
and then just wear a
dress shirt with the vest.

00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:30.143
This is something that is
very well accepted also,

00:11:30.143 --> 00:11:31.660
like in the big consulting firms.

00:11:31.660 --> 00:11:33.253
Also, if you work client-side,

00:11:34.620 --> 00:11:37.520
but some, maybe a bit
more comfortable and comfy

00:11:37.520 --> 00:11:39.690
than maybe the more
traditional suit setup.

00:11:39.690 --> 00:11:41.290
So I like this.

00:11:41.290 --> 00:11:42.350
And probably this is also the reason

00:11:42.350 --> 00:11:44.927
that many other people like this as well.

00:11:44.927 --> 00:11:47.080
- "What's the best advice you would give

00:11:47.080 --> 00:11:49.920
to a business student coming
from your experience?"

00:11:49.920 --> 00:11:52.053
Maybe personal advice?

00:11:53.570 --> 00:11:56.730
- I guess it's probably important to,

00:11:56.730 --> 00:11:59.660
and given that I know that many
people watching this channel

00:11:59.660 --> 00:12:00.493
are interested in consulting,

00:12:00.493 --> 00:12:03.910
it's important to probably
understand rather early

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:07.250
that this is a pathway that you wanna do.

00:12:07.250 --> 00:12:08.930
Because surely if your goal

00:12:08.930 --> 00:12:12.990
is to join one of the big
leading consulting firms,

00:12:12.990 --> 00:12:15.030
you need to really move in that direction

00:12:15.030 --> 00:12:16.200
as fast as possible.

00:12:16.200 --> 00:12:18.160
So I mean, this has to do with grades

00:12:18.160 --> 00:12:19.720
that you need to write,

00:12:19.720 --> 00:12:21.890
so some level of academic performance.

00:12:21.890 --> 00:12:24.670
This has to do with some
internships that you need to make.

00:12:24.670 --> 00:12:26.630
Also, the right cadence of internships.

00:12:26.630 --> 00:12:29.610
I mean, you do need to transform
also your curriculum vitae,

00:12:29.610 --> 00:12:31.630
your pathway in the direction.

00:12:31.630 --> 00:12:35.210
And this level of activities
and of performance

00:12:35.210 --> 00:12:37.460
is maybe not needed if
you are also interested

00:12:37.460 --> 00:12:38.910
in another career path.

00:12:38.910 --> 00:12:41.030
So probably, it's really
about understanding

00:12:41.030 --> 00:12:43.170
what you want to do rather early on,

00:12:43.170 --> 00:12:45.630
and then moving in that way.

00:12:45.630 --> 00:12:46.463
And then of course,

00:12:46.463 --> 00:12:47.980
there are many other
things you can do as well,

00:12:47.980 --> 00:12:51.250
if for whatever reason this
is not what you want to do.

00:12:51.250 --> 00:12:53.170
And I guess that's also very fair,

00:12:53.170 --> 00:12:55.900
and you can have a fantastic
and fulfilling career

00:12:55.900 --> 00:12:58.100
following some of these
other paths as well.

